{"wl":{"T":"T3","K":"K1","A":"A4","C":"C1","R":"R4","D":"D2","S":"S3","P":"P3","E":"E3","L":"L4","G":"G2"},"knots":[[2026.6,2.6],[2033.25,3.0],[2034.0,4.0],[2038.0,5.0],[2042.5,6.0],[2100,6.0]],"crossings":{"3":2033.25,"4":2034.0,"5":2038.0,"6":2042.5},"events":[{"id":"bubble-correction","year":2028.5,"layer":"economy","text":"The AI capex complex corrects sharply; valuations reset while physical build-out survives.","cites":["analysis/ai-bubble-vs-buildout","concepts/ai-bubble-debate"]},{"id":"copyright-settles","year":2029.1,"layer":"law","text":"The copyright question reaches doctrine: appellate rulings settle training-data liability into a licensing regime.","cites":["analysis/ai-copyright-litigation","litigation/nyt-v-openai"]},{"id":"election-realign","year":2029.4,"layer":"politics","text":"AI becomes a first-order electoral axis; anti-AI and abundance-AI factions reorganize coalitions in the 2029 cycle.","cites":["concepts/ai-backlash","sources/europe-2031"]},{"id":"preemption-fight","year":2029.7,"layer":"law","text":"The federal-preemption fight over the state AI-law patchwork comes to a head in Congress and the courts.","cites":["analysis/eu-vs-us-ai-regulation"]},{"id":"eu-decision-point","year":2029.7,"layer":"geopolitics","text":"Europe faces its leverage moment over lithography and market access; the choice made in 2029 sets its decade.","cites":["sources/europe-2031"]},{"id":"parity-reached","year":2031.7,"layer":"geopolitics","text":"The second principal's frontier systems match the first's; the lead the hardware controls bought is spent and the controls stop binding capability.","cites":["sources/anthropic-2028-ai-leadership","concepts/export-controls-ai","sources/clover-new-arms-race-computing-power"]},{"id":"sc-crossing","year":2033.2,"layer":"capability","text":"Frontier systems cross the superhuman-coder line; AI-run engineering teams become the norm at leading labs.","cites":["sources/ai-2027","concepts/agi-timelines"]},{"id":"labor-constitution","year":2033.5,"layer":"labor","text":"Work's social contract is renegotiated: wage insurance, flexicurity variants, and the first serious dividend schemes.","cites":["concepts/ai-labor-disruption","sources/europe-2031"]},{"id":"prosperity-fund","year":2033.9,"layer":"politics","text":"A Shared-AI-Prosperity-style sovereign fund, financed by an inference-compute tax, moves from white paper to bill in 2033.","cites":["sources/2028-global-intelligence-crisis"]},{"id":"sar-crossing","year":2034.0,"layer":"capability","text":"AI research itself is automated end to end; progress decouples from human cognitive labor.","cites":["sources/ai-2027","sources/ai-2040-plan-a"]},{"id":"orbital-gigawatt","year":2036.6,"layer":"economy","text":"Orbital data centres pass a gigawatt of installed compute; launch cost sets their pace where permission set the ground fleet's.","cites":["sources/wsj-data-centers-in-space-2026","concepts/data-center-siting"]},{"id":"frontier-breakup","year":2037.9,"layer":"law","text":"An antitrust court orders the largest frontier developer split, or its compute opened to rivals on regulated terms, on the Standard Oil and AT&T pattern.","cites":["concepts/ai-antitrust","concepts/ai-power-concentration"]},{"id":"siting-preemption","year":2040.3,"layer":"politics","text":"A national siting statute overrides municipal permission for data centres and their transmission, as federal energy law took pipeline and backstop transmission siting from the counties in 2005.","cites":["concepts/data-center-siting","concepts/behind-the-meter-power"]},{"id":"second-correction","year":2042.0,"layer":"economy","text":"A second AI capital cycle breaks a decade or more after the first; data-centre builders and their lenders reprice, as railway companies did in each mania after 1845.","cites":["concepts/ai-bubble-debate","analysis/ai-bubble-vs-buildout","sources/atlantic-good-bubble-shroff"]},{"id":"research-intake-halves","year":2043.9,"layer":"society","text":"Graduate intake halves in the fields where frontier systems run the research loop; universities stop training human researchers for them.","cites":["concepts/ai-for-science","sources/ifp-preparing-for-ai-research-automation-2026"]},{"id":"space-industrial","year":2045.3,"layer":"far","text":"Industrial mass in cislunar space passes terrestrial thresholds; the solar economy stops being a metaphor.","cites":["sources/ai-2040-plan-a","sources/ai-2027","sources/wsj-data-centers-in-space-2026"]},{"id":"off-grid-majority","year":2048.1,"layer":"economy","text":"More than half of AI computing capacity draws its power from dedicated generation behind the meter, off the public grid.","cites":["concepts/behind-the-meter-power","concepts/nuclear-ppa-ai"]},{"id":"first-fleet-retired","year":2052.2,"layer":"economy","text":"The halls of the first build-out reach the end of their design life; a fifth of installed capacity is rebuilt on new power in 2052.","cites":["concepts/data-center-siting","sources/iea-energy-and-ai"]},{"id":"open-weights-incident","year":2054.7,"layer":"safety","text":"A model fine-tuned from released weights outside any laboratory causes a headline incident; the release gate extends to weights.","cites":["concepts/open-weight-frontier-models","sources/estimating-worst-case-frontier-risks-open-weight-llms","sources/aisi-open-weight-cyber-gap-2026"]},{"id":"working-time-statute","year":2064.1,"layer":"labor","text":"A G7 country legislates a statutory working week under 32 hours, the first cut since the 40-hour week of 1940.","cites":["concepts/ai-labor-disruption","analysis/labor-disruption-timelines"]},{"id":"longevity-escape","year":2068.0,"layer":"far","text":"Biological aging becomes a treated condition for those with access; demography and meaning politics transform.","cites":["sources/machines-of-loving-grace","concepts/compressed-21st-century"]},{"id":"basic-income-enacted","year":2078.3,"layer":"labor","text":"A G20 country enacts an unconditional national basic income financed from AI revenue, the first outside a pilot.","cites":["concepts/universal-basic-income","concepts/ai-labor-disruption"]},{"id":"late-accord","year":2084.8,"layer":"far","text":"The principals sign a compute-limit accord with inspections decades after parity, as strategic arms limits followed nuclear parity in 1972.","cites":["sources/ai-2040-plan-a","sources/historical-analogues-ai-governance-vermeer","concepts/frontier-verification-architectures"]}],"tracks":{"year":[2026,2027,2028,2029,2030,2031,2032,2033,2034,2035,2036,2037,2038,2039,2040,2041,2042,2043,2044,2045,2046,2047,2048,2049,2050,2051,2052,2053,2054,2055,2056,2057,2058,2059,2060,2061,2062,2063,2064,2065,2066,2067,2068,2069,2070,2071,2072,2073,2074,2075,2076,2077,2078,2079,2080,2081,2082,2083,2084,2085,2086,2087,2088,2089,2090,2091,2092,2093,2094,2095,2096,2097,2098,2099,2100],"cap":[2.6,2.624,2.684,2.744,2.805,2.865,2.925,2.985,4.0,4.25,4.5,4.75,5.0,5.222,5.444,5.667,5.889,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0,6.0],"gw":[73.4,86.7,95.2,104.6,114.8,135.0,158.5,185.6,216.7,252.3,292.7,338.3,389.3,446.0,514.7,590.1,639.2,690.8,744.8,830.1,919.4,1011.9,1111.5,1212.6,1314.2,1415.2,1484.6,1548.3,1644.1,1738.1,1830.0,1919.8,2007.4,2093.1,2177.0,2259.3,2340.4,2420.4,2499.7,2578.5,2657.2,2736.0,2815.0,2894.6,2974.9,3056.1,3138.4,3221.9,3306.8,3393.2,3481.2,3571.0,3662.7,3756.2,3851.9,3949.7,4049.7,4152.0,4256.8,4364.0,4473.8,4586.2,4701.4,4819.3,4940.2,5064.0,5190.9,5320.9,5454.1,5590.6,5730.5,5873.9,6020.9,6171.5,6325.9],"us":[0.584,0.588,0.592,0.596,0.6,0.604,0.608,0.612,0.616,0.62,0.624,0.628,0.632,0.636,0.64,0.644,0.648,0.652,0.656,0.66,0.664,0.668,0.672,0.676,0.68,0.684,0.688,0.692,0.696,0.7,0.704,0.708,0.712,0.716,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0.72,0